# Tablemarks — private deployment target.
#
# Copy to `docker/.env` and edit. `.env` is excluded from the build context and must never be
# committed.
#
# Nothing here is baked into the image: the app image is built once with no deployment-specific
# hostname in it, and these values are read when the container starts.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the browser reaches PocketBase.
#
# This is a PUBLIC value. It is written verbatim into /config.json, which is served to every
# visitor, and into the app's Content-Security-Policy. Never put a secret in it.
#
# It is the URL the *browser* uses, not an in-network service name: `http://pocketbase:8090`
# resolves only inside the Compose network and will not work from a phone.
#
# Rules enforced at container start (the container refuses to boot otherwise):
#   - must be a plain http(s) URL with no quotes, spaces, semicolons or backslashes
#   - must use https:// unless the host is loopback (localhost / 127.x)
#
# Leave empty for a build with no backend: the app then runs local-only, which is a valid
# state, not an error.
#
# Examples:
#   TABLEMARKS_POCKETBASE_URL=https://pb.example.com
#   TABLEMARKS_POCKETBASE_URL=https://pb.example.com:8090
#   TABLEMARKS_POCKETBASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090
TABLEMARKS_POCKETBASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Silences the nginx entrypoint's per-script log lines.
# NGINX_ENTRYPOINT_QUIET_LOGS=1
